    {
      "issue": "The \"replaced by a plain file\" scenario does not pin that a plain file at an exempt path is recorded. It runs right after the \"re-pointed\" scenario, so at save time the path is a symlink and the snapshot holds a `link:` entry for it. Unlinking that link alone makes the check fail (\"removed\"), whether or not the file put in its place is recorded. A guard that wrongly exempts files, e.g. `LIVE_STATE.has(entry) && !st.isSymbolicLink()` at tests/real-home.mjs:251, passes all 19 scenarios: dir→link is still \"added\", link→link is still \"changed\", link→file is \"removed\". The stated boundary \"a link or file there is still recorded\" is pinned for links only, and the header's claim that \"only the exemption could hide it\" is false for this scenario.",
      "file": "tests/real-home-live-state.mjs",
      "line": "80",
      "quote": "  scenario(`~/.agent-config-studio/${d} replaced by a plain file`, () => {\n    fs.unlinkSync(path.join(T, ACS, d));\n    put(`${ACS}/${d}`, 'a\\n');",
      "suggestion": "Make the file's own entry the only thing that can fail the check: remove the link before the scenario's save (so the path is absent or a real directory in the baseline) and let the mutation create the plain file, and/or add a scenario that edits a plain file already at the path (file → different bytes). Optionally also assert that the check's stdout names the path as added or changed.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 6,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "Every run of `node tests/real-home-live-state.mjs` passes this scenario for the wrong reason. Harm needs a later edit to the exemption condition in tests/real-home.mjs:251 that stops recording a plain file at ~/.agent-config-studio/runs or agents; the suite would stay green.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 12,
      "severity": "medium",
      "filed": false,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f1"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The exemption covers only part of what a review running elsewhere writes under ~/.agent-config-studio. review.mjs's logPath() (packs/review-gate/runtime/review.mjs:598-613) puts review-log.jsonl in ~/.agent-config-studio/review-log whenever that folder exists, and by default on a machine with no older ~/.claude log; line 725 appends a line per review, and security-log.jsonl and eval-log.jsonl sit in the same folder (lines 3529, 5007). That folder is still hashed, so on such a machine a review that finishes during a test run still fails the tripwire in unrelated suites — the flake this branch set out to remove. Unverified on this machine: a glob of ~/.agent-config-studio/review-log/* returned no files, so the log appears to live under ~/.claude here and the path is not reached.",
      "file": "tests/real-home.mjs",
      "line": "85",
      "quote": "const LIVE_STATE = new Set(['runs', 'agents'].map((d) => path.join(HOME, '.agent-config-studio', d)));",
      "suggestion": "Decide whether the review gate's log folder is live state too. If it is, exempt ~/.agent-config-studio/review-log the same way (real directory only) and pin it in tests/real-home-live-state.mjs; if it should stay guarded, say so in the LIVE_STATE comment so the remaining flake is a known one.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 3,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "On a machine whose review log lives in ~/.agent-config-studio/review-log: run ./verify.sh or any suite that calls assertRealHomesUnchanged while a review in another session finishes and appends its log line. Not reached on this machine as far as the glob shows.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 6,
